  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If an arc of \\(45^\\circ\\) on circle \\(A\\) has the same length as an arc of \\(30^\\circ\\) on circle \\(B,\\) then the ratio of the area of circle \\(A\\) to the area of circle \\(B\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{4}{9}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{6}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{4}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "4/9"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2002-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Equal arc lengths give \\(\\dfrac{45}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r_A=\\dfrac{30}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r_B,\\) so \\(45 r_A=30 r_B\\) and \\(\\dfrac{r_A}{r_B}=\\dfrac{2}{3}.\\)\n\nThe ratio of areas is \\(\\left(\\dfrac{r_A}{r_B}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{4}{9}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Arc length is \\(\\dfrac{\\theta}{360}\\cdot 2\\pi r\\)",
        "Equal arc lengths give the ratio \\(\\dfrac{r_A}{r_B}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
